  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "Which of the following is not equal to \\(\\dfrac54?\\)",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{10}{8}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(1\\dfrac14\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(1\\dfrac{3}{12}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(1\\dfrac15\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(1\\dfrac{10}{40}\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "d",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-8-1992-p2.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Note \\(\\dfrac54 = 1\\dfrac14.\\) Now check each choice: \\(\\dfrac{10}{8} = \\dfrac54,\\) \\(1\\dfrac14 = \\dfrac54,\\) \\(1\\dfrac{3}{12} = 1\\dfrac14 = \\dfrac54,\\) and \\(1\\dfrac{10}{40} = 1\\dfrac14 = \\dfrac54.\\)\n\nBut \\(1\\dfrac15 = \\dfrac65 \\neq \\dfrac54.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is D .",
      "hints": [
        "Rewrite \\(\\dfrac54\\) as the mixed number \\(1\\dfrac14\\)",
        "A mixed number \\(1\\dfrac{a}{b}\\) equals \\(\\dfrac54\\) only when \\(\\dfrac{a}{b} = \\dfrac14\\); check each choice"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
